<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bavaria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bavaria is a region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and the country's largest state, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>. Named after the Bavarii, a people first recorded in the 6th century, it was a stem duchy under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agilolfings">Agilolfings</a> and from 1180 was ruled by the Wittelsbach family, who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> in 1623 and kept power until 1918. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> made it a kingdom in 1806, and it joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bavaria.jpg" alt="Bavaria" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: diese Datei: Jwnabd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bavaria_(lozengy).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
